  "description": "High-performance Skia-rendered CollectionView for .NET MAUI (Android). Bakes DataTemplate rows into GPU textures with virtualization, lazy image loading, tap/long-press hit detection, in-cell text editing (Entry/Editor with per-keystroke cell repaint) and a Roslyn source generator that compiles XAML DataTemplates into Skia render trees. Includes Skia counterparts for Border, Grid, Label, Image, StackLayouts, Button, ImageButton (with per-side BorderWidth), Entry, Editor, CheckBox, BoxView, ContentView and ScrollView.",
  "id": "SkiaCollectionView",
  "isPrerelease": true,
  "lastEdited": "2026-10-15T16:22:43.593Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "wff4JaiaGmei1b+1bDIWR3agmR2GkZVoXU+/HdLUzxwQUWxzekFC+QbkxqkUctREVx9lMes4TlwJCZ8braXwmA==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 150257,
  "published": "2026-10-15T16:18:23.797Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.0.0-rc.2 targets .NET 11 / MAUI 11 RC2 (1.4.x targets .NET 10).\nNew: SelectionMode, SelectedItem(s), SelectedItemTemplate and SelectionChangedCommand; CheckBox colors and size (SkiaEx attached properties); rows redraw when their item raises PropertyChanged (ObserveItemChanges); loading placeholders with shimmer; ripple feedback; AutoColumns for grids, with automatic rows in horizontal grids (MinimumItemHeight); ItemAspectRatio; FreezeGcWhileScrolling (CoreCLR) and LogJank diagnostics; font fallback for characters a font lacks; lists keep their gestures inside scrolling parents.\nInteractive template elements (ISkiaInteractiveElement): an element of a baked row takes gestures and is painted live while touched (SkiaMauiControls' SkiaGalleryView uses it). The XAML generator emits template elements of any type that implements ISkiaRenderable.\nLayout: a Start/Center/End Border without a size hugs its content; * rows and columns of a grid in an Auto track keep at least their content size; stack layouts report their size to grids.",
